Rule 1 (input must have floating-point or complex dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10
>>
Rule 2 (out, if provided, must have the same dtype as input to avoid casting errors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (out, if provided, must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 4 (0-dim input implies 0-dim out when provided)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then ndim(v_2) = 0
